      "name": "diagnosis",
      "output": "Between 2026-07-06 00:00:00 and 2026-07-10 21:00:00 \u2014 a 118-hour window \u2014 revenue fell 2.12%. The movement is almost entirely a pricing effect: eCPM came in at 2.2403 against a baseline of 2.4656, a 9.14% decline, accounting for 4.4643 of the share of movement. Requests actually rose 8.59% (1,483,235 vs 1,365,958), offsetting part of the loss at -3.8379 share. Fill rate was essentially flat at 0.7685 vs 0.7746 (-0.79%) and render rate unchanged at 0.9799 vs 0.9800 (-0.01%).\n\nThe drop is localized, and the sharpest cut is ad_format=video: it moved -18.0% against -9.4% globally, carrying 100% of the unexplained movement and 29% of the whole incident. Two correlated slices follow \u2014 os_version Android 12 at -17.2% vs -9.3% globally (73% of unexplained movement, 20% of the incident) and device_model iPhone 14 at -22.3% vs -9.2% globally (66% of unexplained, 18% of the incident). The transition into the window was gradual, not a single step: the largest single hour carried 34% of the change (video eCPM 6.520218 before, 6.102399 after, -0.417818), and it lands exactly on a day boundary. Recovery is also gradual, beginning 2026-07-10 23:00:00 (4.126668 to 4.297747, +0.171079, largest hour 15% of the change), off a day boundary. Interpretation only: a day-aligned, progressive onset over 118 hours is consistent with a rollout, campaign flight, config push or nightly-scheduled job rather than an organic failure.\n\nRuled out: publisher_tier (all 3 values within 0.5% of the global -9.1%, largest outlier 1.1% of the incident), category (all 7 within 3.7% of -9.3%, largest outlier 0.8%), campaign_type (all 4 within 9.1% of -9.1%, largest outlier 0.6%) and vertical (all 8 within 9.1% of -9.1%, largest outlier 0.3%). Region and country are inconclusive \u2014 NAM and US lead their dimensions but each carries 0% of the unexplained movement, under the 50% concentration bar, so the movement is spread rather than concentrated. Fill rate and render rate held steady throughout, so supply and delivery were intact; next step is video demand pricing over 2026-07-06 through 2026-07-10 \u2014 check for campaign flights or bid-config changes that started on the 07-06 day boundary and unwound around 2026-07-10 23:00:00, and confirm whether the Android 12 and iPhone 14 signals are just video inventory concentrated on those slices.",
      "outputPrice": 2.5e-05,
